        "summary": {
          "value": "Inventory: workstations z440 / hp-laptop / hpprodesk + Android SM-A14-5R; Google Workspace plan sam@my-tiny-data-collider.com carries API access (Keep) and future features. Family users Moos, Lola, Menno: engines (then: kernels) exist since many T-days for distributed hyperware/manifold computing, but they have NO Google Workspace identities yet, so no API access to own workspaces and no Keep-note projections to them — DEFERRED. Engines can run on house PCs, in cloud (GCP), in sandboxes (Daytona), or on partial CPU/GPU components; locations are topological in the manifold (at least in MTDC). mo:os = wiring of purpose to operation, governed by access-controlled workspaces (user-id x whether the workspace is on an engine owned by that user); so:om = accumulated skills/tools/scripts/datasets/external code — the I/O for the HG, depending on the ontology surface. Card-granularity ruling: 'what user on what device, running which engine, wants what and why and where-to?'",
