        "summary": {
          "value": "Correction: chrome tabs, Keep instances (Android or workstation), IDEs, and workspace apps (Calendar, Gmail) are NOT surface operations and NOT concurrent processes — they are stateless client/server surfaces any user can access with or without a running engine. The concurrent processes are so:om, in two sorts: (1) processes running the active purpose-wired function sets (a user with access to the workspace whose purpose defines the program structure producing the variable sets for these functions), and (2) processes running external code (skills/tools in other languages) and indexing external processed data (files). Authentication of user-id, device, and workstation-id gates workspace access. Engines run workspaces; all engines together run the manifold; a single-user engine is a manifold on its own (self-similarity). Ontology is governed by the manifold group — for MTDC that is Sam with placeholder coworkers Lola, Moos, Menno — so there is social topology too.",
